From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:50:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0095: the draw's state is built once (P4.4)

Every draw value-initialized a DrawRenderState of 17 KB on its stack: eight color targets of 1.2 KB, three
vertex stages of 2.1 KB, the depth target and the pixel stage. 0088 timed it at ~320 ns a draw, 1.6 ms per
frame in Astro Bot's garden (~5,000 draws), 0.8 ms in FF7 Remake (~2,200).

- The state lives in the RenderExecutor and every draw takes it back (ResetDrawRenderState): the depth
  target, the pixel stage and the scalar fields start over; the tessellation stages only after a
  tessellated draw, which names them; color_info[0] only for the debug dumps, which print it.
- vertex_info[0] and the color targets are left as they were: every draw prepares its vertex stage whole
  (PrepareProgram, PrepareTessellationPrograms), resolves each of its color targets whole
  (ResolveRenderColorTarget) and reads none past color_count.
- 0088's draw state timer times the reset.

The recompiler and the pipeline code are left alone: the shader store keeps its stamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
